AUTHOR     (S.P.Simakov,G.N.Lovchikova,O.A.Sal'nikov,
           A.M.Trufanov,G.V.Kotel'nikova,N.N.Shchadin,
           V.Pilz,H.Foertsch,D.Streil)
TITLE       Cross sections of fast-neutron elastic and inelastic
            scattering on indium isotopes.
FACILITY   (VDGT,4RUSFEI) EGP-10M tandem accelerator -
            Charge exchange electrostatic accelerator in pulse
            operating conditions.
                 Pulse frequency  5 MHz, pulse duration 1 nsec,
                 average proton current  1.5 microAmpere
INC-SOURCE (P-T)
SAMPLE      Hollow cylinders, 4. - 5. cm height, 2.4 -4.5 cm
            outer diameters, wall thickness  0.5 - 0.8 cm
METHOD     (TOF)
DETECTOR   (SCIN)  Stilbene crystal 6.3 cm diam, 3.9 cm height
           Neutron detection efficiency was determined by
           measurement of Cf-252 spontaneous fission neutron
           spectrum described by Maxwellian distribution of
           temperature 1.42 MeV.
MONITOR    (1-H-1(N,EL)1-H-1,,DA) At the angle  45 deg
CORRECTION  Corrections were made on the (p,n) reaction in the
            target, on background, on neutron multiple scattering
            in the samples, on the detector efficiency, on the
            neutron beam attenuation
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T)  Total error
           (ERR-S,2.,8.)  Statistical error 2-8 %
           (ERR-1,10.,20.) Error of the elastic-from-inelastic
                     cross-section  separation  10-20%
           (ERR-2,2.,5.) Detector relative efficiency error 2-5%
           (ERR-3)     Error of the time-to-energy spectra
                       transformation
           (ERR-4)     Multiple scattering correction error
           (MONIT-ERR)     Uncertainty of the monitor CS
HISTORY    (19811130C)
           (19830512U)
           (20151007A) M.M. Ref.of Engl.translation was added.
           STATUS was added in data Subents.
           ERR-ANALYS and COMMON were corrected.
           (20191030U) Two refS.of YK were corrected.
           Two refs of INDC-CCP-169 were added.
           (20200319U) VDG -> VDGT
